# Binaries for programs and plugins
main
vcc
*.exe
*.exe~
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Executables the test suite writes beside its sources: `parser/parser_test.v`
# builds `parser/parser_test`, `pipeline_test.v` builds `pipeline_test`, and
# `tools/gate.vsh` builds `tools/gate`. A `git add -A` in this tree committed
# one of them once, at 2.9 MB; the rules are here so it cannot happen again.
# The sources are `*_test.v`, which the pattern does not match.
#
# The scripts under tools/ are named the same way: `v run tools/build.vsh`
# builds `tools/build` beside it, and a run that stops early can leave its
# scratch directory (`tools/.regress.v3cc.*`) there too. Both are byproducts of
# running a script, and neither is a source.
#
# A plain `v -o vcc .` leaves one of the same shape beside the binary, named for
# it: `.vcc.v3cc.<pid>.<three numbers>`, holding V's generated C. The pattern
# below catches it at the root and under tools/ alike.
*_test
tools/gate
tools/build
tools/bench
tools/compliance
tools/regress
tools/tests
.*.v3cc.*

# Ignore binary output folders
bin/

# Ignore common editor/system specific metadata
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# ENV
.env

# Agent working state: plans, probe scripts, capture generators, scratch notes.
# None of it belongs in history; see AGENTS.md.
.omh/

# Agent and AI tool state. One line per tool that drops a directory in the
# working tree; none of it is project content.
.aider*
.claude/
.codex/
.continue/
.crush/
.cursor/
.gemini/
.goose/
.opencode/
.omo/
.openhands/
.qwen/
.roo/
.windsurf/

# Web assets and local databases
*.db
*.js

# Modules installed with `v install --local` land beside this file, one
# directory per module. Add them here if they should stay out of the repo.
